<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Communist Party of the RSFSR</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1990–1991</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Communist Party of the RSFSR was the branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/communist-party-of-the-soviet-union">Communist Party of the Soviet Union</a> for the Russian republic, founded in 1990, until then the only Soviet republic without a party organisation of its own. Led by Ivan Polozkov, it took a conservative line against Gorbachev's reforms. It was suspended after the failed August coup of 1991, and the Communist Party of the Russian Federation later claimed its succession.</p></div>
